Package: StatARPLS
Title: An R Package for Baseline Correction of Spectra with Automatic Smoothing and Uncertainty
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Taruna", "Dagur", , "tardagur@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides a from-first-principles implementation of Asymmetrically
    Reweighted Penalized Least Squares (ARPLS) baseline correction for
    spectroscopic data. The smoothing parameter is chosen automatically by
    generalised cross-validation, using Hutchinson's stochastic trace
    estimator, and a moving-block residual bootstrap returns a stability band
    that describes how much the fitted baseline varies with the noise. Results
    are returned as an S3 object with print, summary, plot, predict and
    compare methods. The fitting engine is compiled C++ (via 'Rcpp' and
    'RcppArmadillo').
